    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn fractions, mixed numbers and “of”.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A mixed number has a whole part and a fraction part. Convert it to an improper fraction before multiplication or division.\n\nFor example:\n2 1/3 = (2×3+1)/3 = 7/3.\n\nKeeping one fraction form makes later cancellation easier.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
